    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP, the clear centerpiece of today\u2019s lineup is **Corbin Carroll**, who commands a 77.71 efficiency score. Facing Phillips, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a strong order placement at #2 and favorable platoon dynamics, making him our highest-projected asset for both counting stats and the speed we desperately need. **Vinnie Pasquantino** is also a primary start (76.21), bolstered significantly by a 10% wind-out advantage that should aid his power profile against Rocker. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** presents the highest ceiling among our mid-to-late order hitters; he draws a soft matchup against Feltner with a 14% park-factor boost, driving his score to a robust 71.16. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our high-efficiency tier at 69.80, as the park factors in his matchup against Bradish outweigh the relative difficulty of the opposing arm.\n\nOur most critical decision today involves the bottom of the order and bench management. **Austin Riley** (54.71) narrowly edged out a rotation, maintaining his spot despite a lack of recent momentum. **Dalton Rushing**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Zach McKinstry** all occupy the \"marginal\" territory, largely due to unfavorable batting order slots or, in the case of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**, a precarious 38% rain risk that necessitates monitoring. **Cole Young** remains a volatile play; while his 52.70 score is buoyed by a significant park boost against Bradish, his output is capped by facing a high-skill arm and the risk inherent in his pending lineup status. Looking at the bench, we are essentially forced into a defensive posture; with **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, and **Jose Caballero** off-day or inactive, and **Mickey Moniak** sidelined on the IL, we lack the depth to pivot if the weather in the Keller game worsens. We will continue to monitor the status of **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, **Max Muncy**, **Henry Bolte**, **Kyle Karros**, **Carson Williams**, and **Travis Bazzana** for any sudden tactical shifts, but for now, the lineup is set to maximize daily caps while chasing the scarce SB production provided by our top-of-order catalysts.",
